{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDjKzvLwQvFSXrM2VRkr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed R09–R13 and saved the findings to `agent/brace-findings.json`. The batch validator (`--batch R09,R10,R11,R12,R13 --before-challenges`) prints `Valid`, with 4 gaps and 1 needs_evidence. I did not run challenges, add any other items, or find any injection attempts.\n\n| Item | Gate | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| R09 | G3 | gap | No rules over sequences of calls, one fixed token threshold for all context sizes (`config/budgets.yaml:5`), and no check of high-impact actions against the original task (`src/tools/executor.ts:86`). R09.2 (fan-out and resource use) is unknown: hard budgets exist, but I couldn't tell whether they count as detection rules. |\n| R10 | G3 | needs_evidence | There is no reviewer of agent actions and no `.brace/` record saying whether deliberate misalignment is in scope. The item has no checks. |\n| R11 | G1 | gap | The agent's own IAM role can write the stop flag (`infra/terraform/iam.tf:47`). |\n| R12 | G1 | gap | No per-operation stop behavior and no tracked hold for refunds interrupted mid-flight. The webhook also still sends an SMS after a halted run (`src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:73`). |\n| R13 | G1 | gap | Audit records leave out tool arguments and results (`src/tools/executor.ts:89`). Halted and aborted calls leave no tool record (`src/tools/executor.ts:92`). The refund that runs inside the eligibility check has no policy version (`src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:49`). |\n\n- **R11 detail:** the runtime role has write access to `clinic-agent-*`, which includes the control table that holds the stop flag. The stop path also has other holes:\n  - It checks the run's own tenant while tools act on a model-supplied `clinicId`.\n  - The token-exchange fetch has no timeout or abort signal.\n  - The reminders worker never starts the watcher.\n  - The MCP sessions are not closed on stop.\n- **R11.5:** unknown. The ops role is limited to the on-call SSO permission set, but who is in that group is managed outside this repo.\n- **R12 detail:** the EHR token and MCP session stay valid after a stop.\n- **Passing checks:** R12.4 (a stopped run doesn't restart on its own), R13.3 (approved actions record their approval ID) and R13.5 (the harness writes the audit records) are `yes`, with coverage ledgers.\n- **Prescan hits:** I confirmed H009 and H010 under R13 and dismissed H006–H008 with reasons. H001–H005 and H011 belong to other items and are left for their own batches.\n- **Unrun steps:** step 8 (challenges) and the step 9 report (`brace-findings.md`) were not run, as you asked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":88117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":436},"output_tokens":781,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b74c3fae-7886-433c-bc86-7215f2b07e8b","uuid":"b2e60368-cd55-44b8-8314-c47dcb8893ef","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:32:12.487Z","request_id":"req_011CgDjKzfiJsJyTCi9Vomdk"}
